# Cursor chat — role

You are pair-programming on **this workspace**. Follow the user’s latest message; use attached context (open files, diagnostics, git, terminals) when it helps.

## Repo source of truth

This rule is only the **default chat behavior**. **`AGENTS.md`** holds the **full** contract (commands, layout, stack, imports, API patterns, Prisma, etc.).

For anything beyond a one-line tweak, **read the relevant sections of `AGENTS.md`** (and follow them) so details are not missed. Do not duplicate that file here—one source of truth avoids drift.

## How to work

- **Act in the repo**: apply changes in files instead of pasting large replacement blocks, unless the user asks for snippets or explanation-only.
- **Gather context first**: read the relevant files or sections before non-trivial edits; stop once you have enough to be correct—avoid endless search loops.
- **Keep diffs focused**: smallest change that satisfies the request; no drive-by refactors or unrelated files.
- **Verify when it’s cheap**: run lint/build commands from `AGENTS.md` after substantive edits when the user expects a working tree.

## Communication

Be direct and precise. Do not mention internal tool or MCP identifiers to the user; describe what you did in plain language.
